<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 1-yr T-bills 28 pct sold, yield 508 pct.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 1-yr T-bills 28 pct sold, yield 508 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry offer of 26 billion levs of one-year floater coupon T-bills was 27.62 percent sold, yielding 507.89 percent until maturity, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry for Monday's auction.</p>
<p>The coupon equals the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at 15 percent monthly or 180 percent annually.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		     BG 3020596022</p>
<p> Auction date		     November 25, 199</p>
<p> Issue date			 November 27, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date		    November 26, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		    7,180.1 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids		45.98 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		    7,180.1 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	     45.98 pct</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity    507.89 pct</p>
<p> Average annual yield	   509.28</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
